  dialogueText: 'Of course, sometimes you need to politely disagree or say ''no.''

    In
    Ilokano, ''saan'' means ''no.''

    You can use it when you want to give a negative
    response.

    Listen carefully: saan.

    Now, try saying ''saan'' yourself.'
